{"toolCallId":"call_c124ff317e074bb2838acbd35f772ef9","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:115:| REQ-012 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr: quiet mode trims stdout only and never suppresses, redirects, or buffers a stderr warning. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:53:- [ ] T016 Keep stderr out of the quiet branch: leave every warning write on stderr untouched, so `--quiet` trims stdout only and a warning still reaches stderr (REQ-012) (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:67:| AC-013 | REQ-012 | Given an invocation that writes a warning to stderr, When it runs with and without `--quiet`, Then the two stderr captures are byte-identical and quiet stdout still carries only the recommended-level line | `diff <(script <fixture> 2>&1 >/dev/null) <(script <fixture> --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null)` is empty and `script <fixture> --quiet \\| wc -l` returns 1 | Unmet | - |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"2ada7e","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
